## Mission

Close C-II for every sufficiently large triangle-free global minimizer in the canonical normal form, or produce a valid Level I disproof. Do not spend the run re-proving audited extraction/density machinery or optimizing another carrier decimal unless it creates a new implication to global closure.

## Binding normalization

Use the contact-minimal, then diameter-pair-minimal representative and retain every source point, including contact-isolated points.

The §57 ZR/ZF theorem is only on the nonisolated positive-contact core `V`:

\[
\ker\Omega_V=\operatorname{span}\{\mathbf1,P_x|_V,P_y|_V\},
\qquad
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}[V]=2v-3.
\]

Do not extend this affine-kernel theorem to contact-isolated coordinates. Full-source geometry comes from the separate canonical full-source modules.

## Canonical input to treat as solved

Audit.54 is controlling.

Retain all audit.52--53 structure:

- \(\mu_D\ge\mu_{\rm hull}+\varepsilon_*\);
- \(R_F\ge(\kappa_{\rm fr}-o(1))D\);
- \(\sigma_C=0\) and the smooth exact contact manifold;
- the positive reciprocal \((2,3)\)-sparse bounded-end train graph;
- \(|\mathcal O|\ge q-k\);
- simultaneous global face-return quotas;
- joint bulk/face separator capacity;
- terminal short-pocket outer-train depletion and physical wall frustration at its exact scope;
- loaded-flat-pentagon second depletion at its exact scope.

Audit.54 adds two positive theorems.

1. **\`C-EMBEDDED-WALL-REFILL\`.** For pairwise interior-disjoint simple walls of actual unit contacts, let \(S_j\) be the old interior source populations and \(M_j\) certified wall-safe unit-separated refill capacities. If \(T\) covers every actual diameter pair and
   \[
   \boxed{
   \sum_jM_j\ge\sum_j|S_j|+|T|,
   }
   \]
   then there is a same-cardinality unit-separated source with diameter strictly below \(D\).

   In the contact-minimal representative, one wall with enough certified capacity to replace its old interior population already contradicts contact minimality if one deleted interior point carried a contact.

   Exact consequences already canonical:
   - no actual \(7\times7\) unit square contact patch;
   - no \(1/50\)-near-square actual contact perturbation of it;
   - no consecutive affine oblique patch satisfying the audit.54 area inequality.

2. **\`C-PENTAGON-WALL-DISJOINT-BULK\`.** A pentagon-to-pentagon train family can be thinned to pairwise source-vertex-disjoint terminal pentagon walls while retaining a fixed positive fraction of its nonconflicting strict-rhombus crossings.

   In the full-core branch
   \[
   m_B=o(D),\qquad u_B=o(D),\qquad Q-f=o(D),
   \]
   the canonical post-hull-depletion quadratic bulk is asymptotically pentagon-to-pentagon. Therefore there is a family \(\mathcal L\) with
   \[
   \boxed{
   |\mathcal L|=\Omega(D),\qquad
   R(\mathcal L)=\Omega(D^2),\qquad
   |x_\tau-y_\tau|=\Omega(D)\ \forall\tau\in\mathcal L,
   }
   \]
   and all terminal physical pentagon walls are pairwise source-vertex-disjoint.

Two fixed-wall mechanisms are now formally dead:

- \`C-FIXED-WALL-ACTIVATION-REGRESSION\`: positive residual/phase mismatch/KKT rigidity does not imply one fixed-wall spare site, even after deleting one wall point in the finite pentagon packet.
- \`C-LARGE-WALL-LOCK-REGRESSION\`: arbitrarily large near-triangular unit walls with quadratic interior population can still be completely fixed-wall locked.

Do not infer refill capacity from positive residual, near-triangularity, or wall size alone.

## Exact next split

### Full-core branch

The highest-value live route is now **collective movable-wall activation**.

In the low-endpoint-defect branch
\[
m_B=o(D),\qquad u_B=o(D),\qquad Q-f=o(D),
\]
you already have:

- \(\Omega(D)\) macroscopically long stopped trains;
- \(\Omega(D^2)\) retained strict-rhombus crossings;
- pairwise source-vertex-disjoint terminal physical pentagon walls;
- globally disjoint loaded-return paths from exceptional-face defect;
- a smooth exact contact manifold;
- a positive reciprocal train realization;
- the Sections 122--123 detour/payment currency.

The target implication is
\[
\boxed{
\text{collective wall motion/defect}
\Longrightarrow
\text{certified wall-safe packing surplus}
\Longrightarrow
\text{surplus pays an actual diameter cover}
\Longrightarrow
\operatorname{diam}<D.
}
\]

High-value attacks:

1. construct simultaneous finite motions of many disjoint pentagon walls using contact-manifold coordinates while keeping all cross-wall lower constraints valid;
2. prove that long-train/quadratic-crossing coupling forces a positive fraction of those walls to acquire a quantitative refill surplus;
3. route the audit.53 globally distinct loaded returns into a diameter-cover bound compatible with the same wall family;
4. extract a consecutive near-square or sufficiently oblique affine patch so \`C-EMBEDDED-WALL-REFILL\` applies immediately;
5. prove that if the diameter cage blocks all such collective motions, the blocker geometry forces an exact unit equilateral triangle.

Do **not** attempt a universal theorem of the form “positive residual implies one spare point” or “sufficiently large near-triangular wall admits strict refill”; audit.54 contains exact regressions to both.

Outside the low-endpoint-defect regime, first force linear \(m_B\), \(u_B\), or \(Q-f\) to pay against the existing canonical scalar/return ledgers, or reduce back to the wall-disjoint branch.

### Macroscopic inactive-container branch

The new embedded-wall theorem gives the desired endpoint here as well: extract actual unit-contact walls with enough certified packing surplus to replace their interiors and pay an actual diameter cover. The obstacle is now extraction/capacity, not the final source-competitor bookkeeping.

